Between May 3 and May 10, 2024, several macroeconomic events occurred that could influence trading decisions:

1. **U.S. Imposes 25% Tariff on Imported Auto Parts**: On May 3, 2024, the United States implemented a 25% tariff on imported auto parts. However, auto parts manufactured in Canada or Mexico that comply with the United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement (USMCA) were exempted from this tariff. This move could impact the automotive supply chain and trade relations within North America. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_2025_United_States_trade_war_with_Canada?utm_source=openai))

2. **Canada's Trade Deficit Narrows**: In March 2024, Canada's trade deficit with the United States decreased to CAD 506 million, a significant improvement from previous months. This was due to imports falling faster than exports. Notably, exports to the U.S. declined by 6.6%, marking the second consecutive monthly decrease, but this was nearly offset by a 24.8% increase in exports to countries other than the U.S. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_2025_United_States_trade_war_with_Canada?utm_source=openai))

3. **European Markets React to U.S. Tariffs**: On May 3, 2024, European shares fell to a two-month low following the announcement of new U.S. tariffs. The pan-European STOXX 600 index dropped by 1.5%, with German equities leading the decline. Bank stocks were particularly affected, reflecting concerns that escalating trade tensions could hinder economic growth. ([bog.gov.gh](https://www.bog.gov.gh/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/NEWS-BRIEF-03-04-25.pdf?utm_source=openai))

4. **Argentina's Economic Developments**: Argentina secured a $20 billion loan from the International Monetary Fund (IMF), marking a significant improvement in its economic relations after a period of instability. This loan is intended to dismantle remaining capital controls on the peso and bolster the government's reserves. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Javier_Milei?utm_source=openai))

5. **Global Markets Overview**: During the week of May 3 to May 8, 2024, major U.S. stock indices and oil prices experienced modest increases. The Dow Jones Industrial Average achieved its longest winning streak of the year, while the S&P 500 and Nasdaq also saw gains. These movements were supported by healthy corporate profits and weaker-than-expected labor data, which bolstered expectations of potential Federal Reserve rate cuts by the end of the year. ([hlb.com.my](https://www.hlb.com.my/content/dam/hlb/my/docs/pdf/Global_Markets/weekly-market-highlights/2024/10-05-2024.pdf?utm_source=openai))

These events highlight significant shifts in trade policies, economic indicators, and international relations that could influence global markets and trading strategies. 
